========================
Trigonometry & Triangle Formulas
========================

Notation:
---------
Sides: a, b, c
Angles opposite them: A, B, C
Semiperimeter: s = (a + b + c) / 2
Circumradius: R
Inradius: r

====================================
Law of Sines
====================================

a / sin(A) = b / sin(B) = c / sin(C) = 2R

====================================
Law of Cosines
====================================

c² = a² + b² - 2ab cos(C)

b² = a² + c² - 2ac cos(B)

a² = b² + c² - 2bc cos(A)

cos(C) = (a² + b² - c²) / (2ab)

cos(B) = (a² + c² - b²) / (2ac)

cos(A) = (b² + c² - a²) / (2bc)

If the two adjacent sides are adj1 and adj2, and the opposite side is opp:

cos = (adj1² + adj2² - opp²) / (2 × adj1 × adj2)

====================================
Triangle Angle Sum
====================================

A + B + C = 180°

====================================
Right Triangle Ratios (SOH-CAH-TOA)
====================================

sin(A) = Opposite / Hypotenuse

cos(A) = Adjacent / Hypotenuse

tan(A) = Opposite / Adjacent

cot(A) = Adjacent / Opposite

sec(A) = Hypotenuse / Adjacent

csc(A) = Hypotenuse / Opposite

====================================
Angle Sum and Difference
====================================

sin(A + B) = sin(A) cos(B) + cos(A) sin(B)

sin(A - B) = sin(A) cos(B) - cos(A) sin(B)

cos(A + B) = cos(A) cos(B) - sin(A) sin(B)

cos(A - B) = cos(A) cos(B) + sin(A) sin(B)

====================================
Double Angle
====================================

sin(2A) = 2 sin(A) cos(A)

cos(2A) = cos²(A) - sin²(A)

cos(2A) = 2 cos²(A) - 1

cos(2A) = 1 - 2 sin²(A)

tan(2A) = 2 tan(A) / (1 - tan²(A))

====================================
Half Angle
====================================

sin²(A/2) = (1 - cos(A)) / 2

cos²(A/2) = (1 + cos(A)) / 2

tan(A/2) = sin(A) / (1 + cos(A))

tan(A/2) = (1 - cos(A)) / sin(A)

====================================
Product-to-Sum
====================================

sin(A) sin(B)
= (cos(A - B) - cos(A + B)) / 2

cos(A) cos(B)
= (cos(A - B) + cos(A + B)) / 2

sin(A) cos(B)
= (sin(A + B) + sin(A - B)) / 2

====================================
Sum-to-Product
====================================

sin(A) + sin(B)
= 2 sin((A + B)/2) cos((A - B)/2)

sin(A) - sin(B)
= 2 cos((A + B)/2) sin((A - B)/2)

cos(A) + cos(B)
= 2 cos((A + B)/2) cos((A - B)/2)

cos(A) - cos(B)
= -2 sin((A + B)/2) sin((A - B)/2)

====================================
Fundamental Identities
====================================

sin²(A) + cos²(A) = 1

tan(A) = sin(A) / cos(A)

cot(A) = cos(A) / sin(A)

sec(A) = 1 / cos(A)

csc(A) = 1 / sin(A)

====================================
Cosine Identities
====================================

cos(-A) = cos(A)

cos(90° - A) = sin(A)

cos(90° + A) = -sin(A)

cos(180° - A) = -cos(A)

cos(180° + A) = -cos(A)

cos(360° - A) = cos(A)

cos²(A) = (1 + cos(2A)) / 2

1 - cos²(A) = sin²(A)

1 + cos(A) = 2cos²(A/2)

1 - cos(A) = 2sin²(A/2)

====================================
Triangle Area Formulas
====================================

1) Base × Height

Area = (1/2) × base × height

------------------------------------

2) Two Sides and Included Angle

Area = (1/2)ab sin(C)

Area = (1/2)bc sin(A)

Area = (1/2)ac sin(B)

------------------------------------

3) Heron's Formula

s = (a + b + c) / 2

Area = √(s(s - a)(s - b)(s - c))

------------------------------------

4) Using Inradius

Area = r × s

------------------------------------

5) Using Circumradius

Area = abc / (4R)

====================================
Useful Geometry Formulas
====================================

R = a / (2 sin(A))

R = b / (2 sin(B))

R = c / (2 sin(C))

r = Area / s

abc = 4R × Area

Area = r × s
